---
title: Big-batch bolognese
servings: 12
course: dinner
cuisine: Italian
tags: batch, make-ahead, simmered, beef
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/08/recipe-image-legacy-id-1074456_10-1a5351d.jpg?resize=440,400
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/big-batch-bolognese
prep time: 25m
cook time: 1h30m
---

Heat the @olive oil{4%tbsp} in a very large #saucepan{}. Gently cook the @smoked bacon rasher{6}(chopped), @onion{4}(finely chopped), @carrot{3}(finely chopped) and @celery stick{4}(finely chopped) for ~{20%minutes} until golden.

Add the @garlic clove{8}(crushed), @dried mixed herb{2%tbsp}, @bay leaf{2} and @mushroom{500%g}(sliced), then cook for ~{2%minutes} more.

Heat a large #frying pan{} until really hot. Crumble in just enough @beef mince{1500%g} to cover the #frying pan{}, cook until brown, then tip in with the veg. Continue to fry the mince in batches until used up.

Tip the @chopped tomato{2400%g}(6 x 400g cans) and @tomato puree{6%tbsp} in with the mince and veg. Rinse the cans out with the @?red wine{250%ml}(large glass, optional) or with a little water, then add to the #saucepan{} with the @red wine vinegar{4%tbsp} and @sugar{1%tbsp}. Season generously and bring to a simmer. Simmer slowly for ~{1%hour} until thick and saucy and the mince is tender.

Serve with pasta and @parmesan{}(to serve).
